direction: down
title: "C23 PutObjs / MoveObjs graph and opaque tail"
"Shared batch800 plus suffix1" -> "Producer unlock": "last target use of old tail already happened under lock"
"Producer unlock" -> "Consumer lock": "physical release permits acquire; source may still know outcome only as unknown"
"Consumer lock" -> "799 cursor advances": "credit destination, debit shared, follow canonical batch edges"
"799 cursor advances" -> "Destination tail cut": "shared head becomes1202; destination tail1201.next becomes0"
"Destination tail cut" -> "Consumer unlock and pops": "destination head402;800 returns can allocate old tail1201"
"Producer unlock" -> "Source lastPtr overwrite": "use retained401; no read of old target1201; can commute with consumer cut"
"Consumer unlock and pops" -> "Opaque old-tail identity": "payload may be reinitialized; queries need pre-handoff IDs"
"Unknown producer unlock" -> "Stable source supervisor": "cache/activation retained even if consumer drains batch"
"Source lastPtr overwrite" -> "Source receipt and retirement": "known protected publication plus native detachment/finalization"
"Source receipt and retirement" -> "Fresh cache generation": "old metadata cannot authorize access to new cache incarnation"
